      "at": 26.4,
      "question": "What if we lowered the same stone into a liquid denser than water?",
      "choices": [
        "The scale would read less than in water",
        "The scale would read the same",
        "The scale would read more than in water"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "A denser liquid means a bigger Ï, so a bigger buoyant force: the stone seems to lose even more weight."
